Episode 2
Logline: Nadia visits the shell company's address and finds an unexpected witness.
Continuity: Follows Episode 1; Nadia has just learned Halcyon is a shell company.

EXT. DERELICT WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Nadia climbs through a broken window with her phone flashlight.

NADIA
(whispering)
Halcyon Imports. Registered here. There is nothing here.

VOICE
(raspy)
There is plenty here, if you know where to look.

A janitor in a faded cap steps from behind a stack of crates.

NADIA
(startled)
Who are you?

JANITOR
(dry)
I am the man Pruitt pays to keep this building empty.

NADIA
(sharp)
Then why are you talking to me?

JANITOR
(quiet)
Because he stopped paying me three months ago.

He pulls back a tarp. Dozens of unopened boxes labelled with the company logo.

NADIA
(amazed)
These are our products. They were never shipped.

JANITOR
(grim)
He sells the same stock twice and pockets the second payment.

NADIA
(determined)
Will you testify?

JANITOR
(afraid)
I will if you can promise they will not come for my daughter.

Headlights flood the broken window. A car door slams outside.

PRUITT
(calling)
Nadia? I know you are in there. We should talk.
